42619858,\n            \"sha256\": \"6e5eacf500b64292bfb73c49797c1958f6ee44646e43e868039ae7feb573ff75\",\n            \"sha256Source\": \"Vendor-published sidecar asset releases/download/v0.7.1/jadx-headless-mcp.sha256 (98 bytes, one line); the value was independently reproduced here by hashing the downloaded 42,619,858-byte jar. 0.7.1 is the newest release and REA requires exactly this bridge build: the project's own build.gradle.kts documents that the fat jar must be shaded with duplicatesStrategy INCLUDE, otherwise only KotlinMetadataPlugin registers and every APK resolves to a single R class. Versions 0.6.0 and earlier predate that fix.\",\n            \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n            \"moveTo\": \"jadx\",\n            \"saveAs\": \"jadx-headless-mcp-0.7.1-all.jar\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"androidPlatformTools\": {\n      \"description\": \"adb, for REA's device tools. Optional: without a device these tools simply report no devices.\",\n      \"kind\": \"archive\",\n      \"license\": \"Android SDK Terms (Google)\",\n      \"requires\": [],\n      \"optional\": true,\n      \"unpack\": { \"stripRootComponents\": 1, \"moveTo\": \"platform-tools\" },\n      \"probe\": { \"argv\": [\"{vendor}/platform-tools/adb{exe}\", \"version\"], \"expect\": { \"contains\": \"Android Debug Bridge\" } },\n      \"sources\": {\n        \"win32-x64\": {\n          \"version\": \"latest (37.0.1)\",\n          \"url\": \"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-windows.zip\",\n          \"format\": \"zip\",\n          \"size\": 8044989,\n          \"sha256\": \"45f4d63113e895ebde0c90f194099a4676b6ac653bd28d54314a9e022bbc1a99\",\n          \"sha256Source\": \"Google publishes no checksum for this rolling asset; measured on 2026-10-23 and the archive verified readable (15 entries incl. adb.exe). The archive's own platform-tools/source.properties reports Pkg.Revision=37.0.1, so the real pin is 'platform-tools 37.0.1'. Google's repository2-3.xml carries size+checksum for versioned archives if a vendor hash is ever required.\",\n          \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"note\": \"Rolling 'latest' URL pinned by observation; setup re-verifies against this value and reports drift. Android SDK components are not OSI-licensed and Google restricts redistribution, so this is fetched from Google at install time and never re-hosted. Also contains fastboot, sqlite3, mke2fs and the USB API DLLs.\"\n        },\n        \"darwin-x64\": {\n          \"version\": \"latest\",\n          \"url\": \"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-darwin.zip\",\n          \"format\": \"zip\",\n          \"size\": 16110554,\n          \"sha256\": \"ee39ad5967e95c2a07f04dbcbde96b1a0c916ba376096db5d2f498b7727a5d1d\",\n          \"sha256Source\": \"Google publishes no checksum for this rolling asset; measured on 2026-10-23 by downloading the archive and hashing it locally (16,110,554 bytes)\",\n          \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"note\": \"Rolling 'latest' URL pinned by observation; setup re-verifies against this value and reports drift.\"\n        },\n        \"darwin-arm64\": {\n          \"version\": \"latest\",\n          \"url\": \"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-darwin.zip\",\n          \"format\": \"zip\",\n          \"size\": 16110554,\n          \"sha256\": \"ee39ad5967e95c2a07f04dbcbde96b1a0c916ba376096db5d2f498b7727a5d1d\",\n          \"sha256Source\": \"Same darwin archive as x64 (measured 2026-10-23); Google publishes one darwin zip for both architectures.\",\n          \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"note\": \"The darwin archive contains x86_64 binaries. On Apple silicon they run only through Rosetta 2; without it adb cannot start and this optional component is reported unavailable.\"\n        },\n        \"linux-x64\": {\n          \"version\": \"latest\",\n          \"url\": \"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-linux.zip\",\n          \"format\": \"zip\",\n          \"size\": 9054187,\n          \"sha256\": \"d230f13842f60f782a8645f9c813f8f845bf36089ea7289f28c48f17979313f1\",\n          \"sha256Source\": \"Google publishes no checksum for this rolling asset; measured on 2026-10-23 by downloading the archive and hashing it locally (9,054,187 bytes)\",\n          \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"note\": \"The linux archive contains x86_64 binaries. Google publishes no arm64 platform-tools and this bundle does not emulate one, so on linux-arm64 the entry below is offered but its probe is expected to fail — reported as an optional component being unavailable, never as a broken install.\"\n        },\n        \"linux-arm64\": {\n          \"version\": \"latest\",\n          \"url\": \"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-linux.zip\",\n          \"format\": \"zip\",\n          \"size\": 9054187,\n          \"sha256\": \"d230f13842f60f782a8645f9c813f8f845bf36089ea7289f28c48f17979313f1\",\n          \"sha256Source\": \"Google publishes no arm64 platform-tools; this is the same x86_64 linux archive as x64 (measured 2026-10-23), recorded so the mismatch is explicit instead of implied.\",\n          \"sha256VerifiedOn\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"note\": \"Kept so an arm64 host reports a precise failure instead of \\\"no source\\\". adb here is x86_64: it runs under qemu/binfmt where the host provides it, and otherwise the probe fails and the report names it.\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"reaAgents\": {\n      \"description\": \"The REA MCP server itself, installed into vendor/node_modules so the bundle owns the runtime copy. The resolved entry point is vendor/node_modules/rea-agents/scripts/rea.mjs.\",\n      \"kind\": \"npm\",\n      \"license\": \"MIT\",\n      \"requires\": [\"node\"],\n      \"unpack\": { \"moveTo\": \"rea-agents\" },\n      \"probe\": {\n        \"argv\": [\"{node}\", \"{vendor}/node_modules/rea-agents/scripts/rea.mjs\", \"--version\"],\n        \"expect\": { \"regex\": \"^6\\\\.8\\\\.0(\\\\s|$)\" }\n      },\n      \"sources\": {\n        \"npm\": {\n          \"version\": \"6.8.0\",\n          \"registry\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/rea-agents\",\n          \"integrity\": \"npm's own dist.integrity is the authoritative check for this tarball: the registry tarball ships NO node_modules (verified: 2398 entries in 6.8.0, 0 under node_modules), so setup resolves the dependency closure with `npm install --ignore-scripts` instead of unpacking a tarball.\",\n          \"note\": \"`just unpacking the published tarball cannot work` is a verified fact, not a caution: the CLI would fail with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND on zod. 6.8.0 (published 2026-10-25, npm latest; 6.6.0 was never on npm) does raise the runtime floor: engines.node went from ^22.19.0 || ^24.11.0 || >=26.0.0 to ^22.23.4 || ^24.22.1 || >=26.12.1, which makes the pinned Node 24.22.1 exactly the floor of its line — hence pins.nodeEngines and the node probe had to move with it. bin is still scripts/rea.mjs, and the dependency closure gained exactly two packages (@bufbuild/protobuf 2.16.0, @msgpack/msgpack 3.1.3), so the same npm install path resolves it. This one IS a tool expansion: the shipped dist/mcp-catalog.json records identity.counts = 229 MCP tools / 175 CLI commands / 6 prompts (6.7.0 shipped no catalog and exposed 207), with new families for APK signatures, binary diagnostics, model artifacts (GGUF/safetensors) and CUDA/HIP code objects. The two version gates this bundle cares about did NOT move: SUPPORTED_GHIDRA_VERSION is still 12.1.4 (so Ghidra 12.2 is still unsupported) and JADX_RELEASE is still 0.7.1 with the same 6e5eacf5… sha256 (so jadx 0.8.0 is still rejected) — those pins stay put.\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"notProvisionable\": {\n    \"$comment\": \"Upstream host gates. Listed so the setup report can explain an unavailable capability instead of silently omitting it.\",\n    \"hopper\": \"macOS only (HOPPER_LAUNCHER_PATH).\",\n    \"ida\": \"requires a user-owned IDA plus REA_IDA_MCP_CONFIG; REA never launches IDA.\",\n    \"firmware\": \"binwalk/unblob are Linux-only (REA_BINWALK_COMMAND / REA_UNBLOB_COMMAND).\",\n    \"wakaru\": \"Linux x64 only (REA_WAKARU_COMMAND).\",\n    \"pwntools\": \"Linux x64 only (REA_PWNTOOLS_PYTHON) — ELF layout and recorded-crash tools.\",\n    \"pwndbg\": \"Linux/macOS only (gdb + REA_PWNDBG_GDB).\",\n    \"mitmdump\": \"Linux only, native mitmproxy captures (REA_MITMDUMP_COMMAND); HAR needs no engine.\",\n    \"appleToolchain\": \"macOS only (xcrun, plutil, assetutil, hdiutil, lldb).\",\n    \"processCapture\": \"Linux/macOS PTY only.\",\n    \"ilspycmd\": \"Optional .NET decompiler (REA_ILSPY_CMD_PATH). Only wired when a runnable ilspycmd already exists; the static managed provider works without it.\",\n    \"browser\": \"Reused from the host (REA_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE). Never downloaded by this bundle.\"\n  }\n}\n"
